Page 1 of 4

A storm has wedged loose coral across the reef nursery. Octo-Pop promises the tiny fish
he will clear a safe path before the strong current returns.
Page 2 of 4

He carries two stones in four arms and steadies the coral with four more. Then
Cereal-Swimmer arrives clutching the nursery’s guiding pearl.
Page 3 of 4

A wave knocks the pearl into a narrow crack. Octo cannot reach it while holding the reef,
so he asks the smallest fish to form a passing chain.
Page 4 of 4

The chain returns the pearl one fin at a time, and its glow guides everyone through. Eight
strong arms saved the reef; many small fins saved its light.
Questions for Octo-Pop’s Coral Reef

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: Why must Octo-Pop clear the reef quickly?
Page 2
Talk together: How does Octo-Pop use all eight arms?
Page 3
Talk together: Why does Octo-Pop need the tiny fish?
Page 4
Talk together: What does the rescue show about different kinds of strength?
After reading
How did the fish recover the pearl?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: They formed a passing chain.

